WEBVTT

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:02.020
Boss?

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:03.440
At your service.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.490
Oh, hello. Nice to meet you.

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:08.400
You talked!

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.490
Huh? Does he usually not talk so much?

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.220
This is the first time I've heard him speak!

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.390
How?! Wait, could you talk all along?!

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:21.750
What is your name? 
What would you like to see?

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:28.590
M-My name is Kaban. 
I'd like to see the library.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:32.940
Understood. I will search 
for a route to the library.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:36.890
But first, I will tell you about Japari Park.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:42.720
Japari Park is divided into several Areas 
based on different environments.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.980
Each Area displays animals and 
plants native to its climate.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:50.070
First, the park is broadly divided 
into five climate zones.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.480
The creatures in the park 
are called "Friends,"

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.930
and they are animals or their vestiges...

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:05.580
Ahem. Testing, testing.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.750
Huh?

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.650
Testing, testing.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:11.750
Can you hear me now? 
This is the Savanna Area.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.470
Fell asleep, huh?

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:27.010
You've had a long day, Kaban-chan. 
It must have worn you out.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:33.650
That really surprised me. 
I never knew you could talk, Boss.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:38.030
You have a funny voice, huh?

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.730
I bet everybody would love to talk to you.

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:44.940
How come you've never talked before?

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.210
Come on, say something!

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:27.510
Where am I?

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:35.020
Please don't eat me!

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.900
Come on, I won't eat you!

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:38.790
Good morning!

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:42.250
S-Sorry, Serval-chan. Good morning.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:44.250
You fell asleep on us yesterday.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.440
Huh? Did I?

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:47.780
Yesterday...

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:51.540
Good morning, Kaban. Shall we depart?

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.040
You talked again!

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:06.630
To confirm, your destination 
is the Japari Library, correct?

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:12.380
Yes. I'd like to look up 
what kind of animal I am.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.450
And I'm the chaperone!

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:20.480
Understood. Searching for 
a route to the library.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:32.600
Japari Library is in the Forest Area.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:35.140
You will pass through three Areas on the way.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:40.180
However, it is a very long distance. 
Walking is not recommended.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.630
Let's take the Japari Bus.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:48.140
The closest bus is next to the Unin Bridge.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:50.830
A bus?

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:52.810
What's a bus?

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.440
A bus is a type of vehicle.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:59.120
The Japari Bus makes touring 
this large park a cinch.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.730
Wow...

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:05.240
I recommend a scenic walk through 
the jungle until we reach the bus.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.000
Is that acceptable?

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.070
Yes!

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:11.180
I will now begin the tour.

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:14.340
The tour will last about two hours.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:15.610
All right!

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:36.940
It's so different from the savanna.

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:41.570
The Jungle Area has a 
tropical rain forest climate.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:45.270
There are also many animals.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:51.720
You can hear all kinds of sounds. 
Maybe we'll meet more Friends today!

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:58.390
Found one!

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:00.710
Over there. Look, on the tree branch.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:03.590
She looks like you, Serval-chan.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:05.630
That is an ocelot.

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:08.970
Order: Carnivora
Family: Felidae
Genus: Leopardus

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.970
Like the serval, they belong to the cat family.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:14.340
Because they are nocturnal, they rest in 
trees or in the brush during the daytime.

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:16.790
They are also excellent tree-climbers.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:23.510
Lucky! I want to take a nap, too.

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:25.730
There's something over there, too.

00:06:28.390 --> 00:06:32.690
A Malayan tapir. They have a 
unique black and white pattern.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:41.750
Order: Perissodactyla
Family: Tapiridae
Genus: Tapirus

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:38.860
At nighttime, the white part stands out, 
making their outline vague.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:40.900
This makes them difficult to spot.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.050
What a strange pattern.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:46.580
There are so many different kinds of Friends.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:58.390
Order: Carnivora
Family: Eupleridae
Genus: Cryptoprocta

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:53.300
Huh? I don't recognize you.

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:58.390
Are you Serval, the serval?

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:00.890
You know me?

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:04.450
Of course. You're famous!

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:08.130
You know, the Savanna Area troublemaker!

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:10.570
I'm not a troublemaker!

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:12.350
I'm Fossa.

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:16.360
I live around here, but I go to the 
Savanna Area once in a while, too.

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:20.320
Long tail, isn't it?

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:22.270
Who's she?

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:26.940
She's Kaban-chan. We going to the library 
to find out what kind of animal she is.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:30.380
Wow, what a long trip. That sounds rough.

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.200
Take care, now.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:33.270
Thanks!

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:35.050
Thank you very much.

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:39.730
She looked strong.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:43.650
She was so big! And her tail...

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:49.660
I'm sorry. I danced right into you.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:51.990
Order: Proboscidea
Family: Elephantidae
Genus: Elephas

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:51.990
O-Oh, no! I'm the one who bumped into you.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:55.020
The sunlight filtering through the 
foliage here is beautiful, isn't it?

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:57.950
Dancing puts me in such a good mood.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.610
She's so big.

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:03.450
The Indian elephant is a 
subspecies of Asian elephant.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:07.330
Along with the African elephant, 
it is the largest land animal.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.120
Bye, now.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.180
See you again!

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:11.210
Goodbye.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:16.110
That was an even bigger Friend.

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:17.800
And kinda showy, too.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:20.110
Oh, there's someone else.

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:22.290
What are you doing?

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:27.110
Order: Artiodactyla
Family: Cervidae
Genus: Axis

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:27.110
Licking this dirt is good for you.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:31.150
It's something about the... "salt"?

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:33.490
Why don't you two try it?

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:35.510
Huh? Really?

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:38.650
Um, maybe another day.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:42.900
I'm King Cobra.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:45.140
Order: Squamata
Family: Elapidae
Genus: Ophiophagus

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:45.140
What is it? Need a favor?

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:49.190
Order: Pilosa
Family: Myrmecophagidae
Genus: Tamandua

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:49.190
Wh-What do you want? Go away!

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.110
Order: Galliformes
Family: Phasianidae
Genus: Pavo

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.110
I'm Peafowl.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:53.320
I'm Tasmanian Devil!

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:53.530
Order: Dasyuromorphia
Family: Dasyuridae
Genus: Sarcophilus

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:55.320
Whoa, you scared me!

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:54.880
Order: Squamata
Family: Agamidae
Genus: Chlamydosaurus

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:56.910
Order: Artiodactyla
Family: Giraffidae
Genus: Okapia

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:56.760
I'm Okapi!

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:01.020
Wow, there really are lots of Friends here.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:02.340
Yeah, really.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:07.820
But the heat here isn't quite 
like the heat in the savanna.

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:09.110
You're right.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:13.990
The Jungle Area is constructed 
to be a tropical rainforest.

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:17.130
The treetops form a canopy layer.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:22.490
There are also many kinds of flora that 
make use of other trees, like vines.

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.350
It's gotten thick.

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:33.340
Serval-chan!

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:38.030
Thanks. You're really dexterous, Kaban-chan.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:41.650
Boss!

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:42.290
Lucky-san!

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:57.000
Hey, Boss, are we going the right way?

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.480
The path's getting smaller and smaller.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:06.030
Leave it to me. The whole map 
of the park is in my head.

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:10.830
Once we exit this brush, the rest 
of the walk will be a breeze.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:12.430
All right! Let's go!

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:25.540
Huh?

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:27.270
This is...

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:34.610
L... L-L-L-Leave it to... L-L...

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:31.370
Lucky-san?

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:31.370
Boss?

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:33.270
What's going on?

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.610
Where's the path?

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:38.300
Now what?

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:44.740
Made it!

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:46.610
Whee!

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:49.160
So fun!

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:58.590
So fun!

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.090
Hellooo!

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:00.760
Huh?

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:08.890
I'm Small-clawed Otter. 
Perfect day for sliding, isn't it?

00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:08.890
Order: Carnivora
Family: Mustelidae
Genus: Amblonyx

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:11.350
Are you here to play, too?

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:15.870
Nope. We were walking,
but the path disappeared here.

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:17.980
Do you know where it is, Otter?

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:21.250
I've never seen anyone come this way before.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:23.950
It's been my playground for a long time.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:27.900
Okay, one more slide!

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:29.210
Wait, wait!

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:32.280
Excuse me! We're looking for the Unin Bridge.

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:34.420
Do you happen to know anything about it?

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:39.340
Well, Jaguar-chan passes through here. 
Why don't you ask her for a ride there?

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:41.340
A ride?

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:44.750
That's tons of fun, too!

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:48.720
I mean, I can swim by myself, 
but I end up riding anyway.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:51.520
When does this Jaguar pass through here?

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:55.400
I dunno. About twice a day?

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:57.970
You could sunbathe while you wait.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.910
Whatever you're doing, it looks 
like fun! I wanna try it, too!

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:17.510
Fun, right? See, it's fun, right?

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:19.070
I can do this, too.

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:20.880
Oh, wow. You're so dexterous.

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:24.610
And then like this. Like this.

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:28.600
Yeah! You've got it, you've got it!

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:31.620
Wait, wait!

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:33.060
Let us on!

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:37.570
The otters are very curious, 
so they're quick to approach people.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:13:02.940
Toubu Zoo: Kudou-oneesan (Saitama Prefecture)

00:12:37.570 --> 00:12:40.520
Visitors will stretch their hands 
out toward the otters,

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:43.400
and the otters want to touch them.

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:48.100
The otters' paws are soft, so it's 
not as if they'll attack with claws.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:53.520
They can dive all the way to the bottom 
of a river and are powerful divers,

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:56.310
so in the summertime,
they mostly swim in the pool.

00:12:56.310 --> 00:13:00.550
Then, when they want a nap, they'll dry 
themselves, take an afternoon nap,

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:03.090
and then go back in the pool again.

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:10.080
I've never done this before!

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:12.220
It's incredible.

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:17.980
Order: Carnivora
Family: Felidae 
Genus: Panthera

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:17.980
You want to go to Unin Bridge, right?

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:20.430
Thanks! You're a big help!

00:13:20.430 --> 00:13:22.720
When the path disappeared, 
we didn't know what to do.

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:26.220
The river changes shape in this area.

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:30.390
I'm sorry. Isn't this hard work?

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:33.410
I'm fine! Leave it to me.

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:37.310
The jaguar is unusual among
cats in that it can swim.

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:38.620
That's right!

00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:41.550
Wait, Boss, you can talk?

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.780
Is that why you do this job?

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:47.880
Yup, there were a lot of girls 
who needed to cross but couldn't.

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:50.760
Plus, the view from here is great.

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.990
Okay, we're going out into the main river!

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:58.700
It's big! It's so big!

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:00.980
Yeah, it's so wide!

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:03.670
That's the Unin Bridge!

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:07.670
There we go.

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:14.480
This way. This way.

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:16.040
It is just up ahead.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:22.140
We did it!

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:26.150
This is a bus?

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:29.100
Cool! Cool!

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:32.370
It's so big.

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:34.880
Hey, Boss, can I touch it? 
I can touch it, right?

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:36.440
I want to ride on top of it!

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:39.640
Can I? Yay, bus, bus!

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:41.530
It feels so strange.

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:43.660
Yahoo! I'm on top of the bus!

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:44.650
Sniff, sniff.

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:46.330
The driver's seat is missing.

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:48.610
What? Driver's seat?

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:52.290
Searching for driver's seat.
Searching for driver's seat.

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:56.040
There should also be a frame here.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:59.770
Searching for driver's seat.
Searching for driver's seat.

00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:59.770
Wait, if it doesn't have that, is it not a bus?

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:06.050
I've seen something similar to this 
on the other bank. Maybe that's it?

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:10.610
Wonderful.

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:12.520
This is it. This is it.

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:14.260
Oh, glad I could help!

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:16.740
What a funny shape!

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:19.240
So this is what it is.

00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:21.350
This attaches to the other part, huh?

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:27.110
But how do we move this across the river?

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:31.150
Stare...

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:32.100
Really?

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:42.770
This won't work. It's too heavy.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:47.010
Serval, aren't you're good at jumping? 
Can't you carry it over?

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:55.130
How about we all try holding 
it up while we swim over?

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:57.240
Whee! It's sinking!

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:59.350
Huh? Kaban-chan?

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:01.110
Where's Kaban-chan?!

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:09.940
This is a little too much for us.

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:13.020
I've never carried anything 
this heavy before.

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:15.610
I'm so sorry. Because of me...

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:17.450
It's okay. Let's do our best.

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:19.950
I want to see the completed bus, too.

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:24.750
Hmm... But the river's just too big.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:26.930
There's a lot of water right now.

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:30.920
Huh? Hey, where does that road go?

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:35.880
Um, to the Desert Area. On this side,
it goes to the Savanna Area.

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:38.830
Wow. It looks like a lot of 
girls pass through here.

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:42.530
Yeah, there are so many girls 
who want to cross. It's hard work.

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:46.420
I wonder what everyone did
before you came along, Jaguar.

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:50.620
Not sure... Maybe they had the girls who 
could swim carry them on their backs?

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:54.050
Um, I have an idea.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:55.920
Huh? What is it?

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:58.180
It might be a lot of work, though...

00:16:58.860 --> 00:16:59.810
I don't mind.

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:01.930
Sounds fun. I'm in!

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:20.170
First, Jaguar-san, 
can you take this to Otter-san?

00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:21.600
Gotcha.

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:24.600
Jaguar! Hurry, hurry!

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:29.770
Got it, Kaban!

00:17:30.260 --> 00:17:36.090
Next, can you loop it behind the pole
and hand it back to Jaguar-san?

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:38.110
Okay!

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:42.230
This is fun! It's weird! It's so weird!

00:17:42.230 --> 00:17:43.710
Here, Jaguar.

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:45.810
Roger that.

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:49.670
Here.

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.170
Thank you.

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:54.610
What next?

00:17:54.610 --> 00:17:56.310
We pull this.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:08.190
It's moving! It's moving!

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:25.250
Otter-san, could you hook 
that loop over the post?

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:30.130
So heavy, but so interesting!

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:40.850
What is this? What is it, what is it?

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:43.240
Wow. How curious.

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:46.690
Could I ask you to do this three more times?

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:48.100
Yeah!

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:01.120
Okay, I'd like to test it.

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:03.580
Me, me! I wanna go!

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:06.490
Okay, here goes!

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:18.250
Me next! I wanna do it!

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:20.620
That's incredible. It's like magic.

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:24.230
Isn't it? Kaban-chan is really amazing!

00:19:25.690 --> 00:19:28.110
Okay, it's time for the real thing.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:53.780
Let's go!

00:19:59.020 --> 00:20:00.770
We did it!

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:07.720
Boss, this should do it, right?

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:10.840
Okay, here goes! One, two...

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:16.250
It's a bus!

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:18.860
Did we make a bus? Is it a bus now?

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:20.610
I... have no idea.

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:22.450
Do we get on? Do we get on?

00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:22.820
What's Boss doing?

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:25.140
Lucky-san, what are you doing?

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:27.340
I have no idea what's going to happen.

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:41.980
Huh?

00:20:43.170 --> 00:20:44.840
It went quiet.

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:45.800
Yeah.

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:47.780
Huh? Did it die?

00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:49.330
Is the bus dead?!

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:51.140
Maybe it's just asleep?

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:55.620
I see. It seems that the battery is dead.

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:58.270
Huh? What's a battery?

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:01.110
This is a battery.

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:04.700
It seems to be empty now.

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:09.580
I don't really get it.
Does that mean we can't play?

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:12.790
Is there any way we can charge it?

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:19.310
It can be charged on the roof of Japari Café, 
at the top of the mountain over there.

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:36.950
H-How are we going to get up there?

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:40.690
Huh?

00:23:11.840 --> 00:23:41.290
Tennouji Zoo: Nakayama-oniisan (Osaka)

00:23:11.940 --> 00:23:16.570
Jaguars have large faces, 
thick necks, short legs,

00:23:16.570 --> 00:23:20.980
and sturdy bodies that are 
sort of stout and plump.

00:23:20.980 --> 00:23:24.670
They need to climb trees and swim,

00:23:24.670 --> 00:23:29.160
so they have bodies that 
let them hunt anywhere.

00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:35.410
Leopards have round rosettes 
scattered on their fur,

00:23:35.410 --> 00:23:41.440
but jaguars also have dots 
inside the rosettes.

00:23:41.880 --> 00:23:43.320
PPP Preview!

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:45.760
This week, we'll introduce the alpaca.

00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:46.720
Alpaca?

00:23:46.720 --> 00:23:48.220
Apparently, they spit.

00:23:48.220 --> 00:23:49.640
Does that mean they're attacking?

00:23:49.640 --> 00:23:50.590
Maybe it's an expression of affection?

00:23:50.590 --> 00:23:52.180
Is it marketing? Not marketing...

00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:52.980
Marketing?

00:23:52.980 --> 00:23:54.560
Marking!

00:23:54.560 --> 00:23:56.410
Next time, "Mountain."
